"entity": {
"name": "Coeur Mining, Inc.",
"description": "Coeur Mining, Inc. engages in the well-diversified, growing precious metals producer with a focus on generating sustainable, high-quality cash flow and returns from a balanced, prospective asset base in mining-friendly jurisdictions along with commitment to exploration and expansions. It operates through the following segments: Palmarejo, Rochester, Kensington, Wharf and Silvertip. The Palmarejo segment includes a gold-silver complex. The Rochester segment operates an open pit heap leach silver-gold mine in northwestern Nevada. The Kensington segment relates to an underground gold mine located north of Juneau, Alaska. The Wharf segment focuses on an open pit heap leach gold mine located near Lead, South Dakota. The Silvertip segment silver-zinc-lead exploration located in the state of Sonora in northern Mexico. The company was founded in 1928 and is headquartered in Chicago, IL.",
"rbics_econ": "Non-Energy Materials",
